abstract: >
  YARF is a customizable, asynchronous, and parallelized random forest
  implementation for R. It supports user-defined JavaScript splitting and
  aggregation behavior, missingness incorporated in attributes,
  random-forest-based imputation, variable importance, interaction analysis,
  and tree inspection. Its forest engine is implemented in Java.
